    },
    {
      "slide_id": "masterclass-2",
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "curated",
      "heading": "2 · Show the process",
      "sentence": "Prompts, selection decisions, and re-authoring belong in the portfolio — not only the polished output.",
      "quote": "Screen-glow winter.\nA thousand options. No taste.\nWho closed the door?",
      "quote_origin": "tao_invented",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Tao of Creativity)",
        "href": "/creativity-techniques-uem/lessons/en/creativity-techniques/u-5-creativity-technology/#tao-of-creativity"
      },
      "image_brief": "Show the process: reprogramming is visible labour, not a magic prompt.",
      "notes": "- Process transparency is a design ethic, not a software feature.\n- Record what you asked, what you kept, and what you rejected.\n- Assessment should be able to read your judgment, not only your render.\nSource: course wording; fieldlex process transparency.\nAsk: What would a critic miss if they saw only your final file?",
      "claims": [],
      "asset_id": "wikimedia:File:Reprogramming ENIAC.png",
      "media_slot_id": "U5.masterclass-2"
    },
    {
      "slide_id": "masterclass-3",
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "curated",
      "heading": "3 · Refuse originality theatre",
      "sentence": "Fast, pretty outputs without problem framing are empty craft — they perform novelty without a brief.",
      "image_brief": "Refuse originality theatre: a polished machine surface is not a design argument.",
      "notes": "- High speed can hide weak framing.\n- Originality theatre looks creative but answers no question.\n- Name the problem before you celebrate the surface.\nSource: course wording; Pass-1 discourse on originality theatre.\nAsk: Which output this week was pretty but untethered to a question?",
      "claims": [],
      "asset_id": "wikimedia:File:UNIVAC-FILE-COMPUTER-BRL61-0944.jpg",
      "media_slot_id": "U5.masterclass-3"
